t.js with GitHub integration.  \\\\n• Use Render Blueprints for Strapi + managed Postgres.  \\\\n• Provision S3 bucket via Terraform (or Pulumi) and IAM user.  \\\\n• Maintain staging/prod environments, backups, monitoring (Render & Vercel logs, UptimeRobot, Sentry).  \\\\n• Update cost estimate accordingly (target ≤ $35/mo).  \\\\nReturn REPORT with sequence ID devops-sync-v2.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"devops-sync-v2\\\"\\n}\\n###order_devops_sync###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-26T18:47:08.656Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_arch_sync\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order arch-sync-v2 from agent 5: ## Unified Architecture – HOA Website\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 1. Locked-In Technology Stack\\\\\\\\n• **Front-End** – Next.js (React + TypeScript) on Vercel (SSG for public, SSR for resident-only pages).  \\\\\\\\n• **CMS / API** – Strapi v4 (Node.js) on Render.com w/ managed PostgreSQL.  \\\\\\\\n• **Authentication** – Auth0 (OIDC/JWT).  \\\\\\\\n  – Residents authenticate through Auth0 Universal Login; Next.js fetches an ID-token & access-token.  \\\\\\\\n  – Strapi endpoints validate Auth0 access-tokens (resident CRUD) via JWKS.  \\\\\\\\n  – Strapi **admin** login continues to use native credentials (isolated `/admin` realm).  \\\\\\\\n• **File Storage** – AWS S3 bucket (`hoa-files`)  \\\\\\\\n  – Prefix `/public` (world-read) fronted by CloudFront.  \\\\\\\\n  – Prefix `/private` requires time-limited signed URLs generated by Strapi.  \\\\\\\\n• **CI/CD** – GitHub Actions → Vercel & Render.  \\\\\\\\n• **Monitoring** – UptimeRobot + Sentry.  \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 2. Key Modules / Services\\\\\\\\n1. **Public Website** (Next.js) – Home, About, Contact, Amenities.  \\\\\\\\n2. **Resident Portal** (Next.js SSR) – Dashboard, profile, announcements, documents.  \\\\\\\\n3. **CMS / API** (Strapi) – Content types, media library, role-based permissions.  \\\\\\\\n4. **Auth Layer** – Auth0 tenant, SPA + M2M applications, JWKS endpoint, RBAC roles: `resident`, `board`.  \\\\\\\\n5. **Storage** – S3 + CloudFront; signed URL service in Strapi `/docs/signed-url`.  \\\\\\\\n6. **CI/CD & Monitoring** – GitHub Actions workflows, Sentry SDKs, UptimeRobot.  \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 3. Cross-Director Integrations\\\\\\\\n• DNS/Email Director – Domain records, Postmark SMTP creds for Auth0 email + Strapi reset.  \\\\\\\\n• Security/Compliance Director – Review Auth0 tenant config, S3 IAM policy, JWT expiry.  \\\\\\\\n• Payments Director (optional) – Stripe keys if dues payment added later.  \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 4. Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)\\\\\\\\n`(V)` = deterministic value captured, reuse later `(NV)` = non-deterministic generated value noted.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n0. **Prerequisites**  \\\\\\\\n   Repo `hoa-site` (front-end) and `hoa-cms` (back-end) exist in GitHub org.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **Auth0 Tenant Setup**\\\\\\\\n1.1  Create tenant `hoa-prod` (NV: TENANT_ID).  \\\\\\\\n1.2  Create **SPA Application** `hoa-next`  \\\\\\\\n     – Callback URL `https://hoa.example.org/api/auth/callback/auth0`  \\\\\\\\n     – Allowed Logout URL `https://hoa.example.org/`  \\\\\\\\n     – Capture `CLIENT_ID`, `CLIENT_SECRET` (V).  \\\\\\\\n1.3  Create **M2M Application** `hoa-strapi`  \\\\\\\\n     – Authorize to Management API `read:users`  \\\\\\\\n     – Capture `M2M_CLIENT_ID`, `M2M_CLIENT_SECRET` (V).  \\\\\\\\n1.4  Define roles `resident`, `board` in Auth0 RBAC. (deterministic).  \\\\\\\\n1.5  Enable RBAC & add custom claim `https://hoa/roles` in tokens.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. **Front-End (Next.js)**\\\\\\\\n2.1  `npx create-next-app@latest hoa-site --typescript`.  \\\\\\\\n2.2  Add Auth0 SDK: `npm i @auth0/nextjs-auth0`.  \\\\\\\\n2.3  Configure `.env.local`  \\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_SECRET=(NV openssl rand -hex 32)\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_BASE_URL=https://hoa.example.org\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_ISSUER_BASE_URL=https://${TENANT_ID}.us.auth0.com\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_CLIENT_ID=${CLIENT_ID}\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET=${CLIENT_SECRET}\\\\\\\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.hoa.example.org\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n2.4  Implement API proxy route `/api/token` to exchange and silently refresh tokens for Strapi calls.  \\\\\\\\n2.5  Protect resident pages with `withPageAuthRequired` HOC.\\\\\\\\n2.6  Commit & push to GitHub.  \\\\\\\\n2.7  Vercel import repo → project `hoa-site`  \\\\\\\\n     – Record `VERCEL_PROJECT_ID` (V).  \\\\\\\\n     – Set env vars from step 2.3.  \\\\\\\\n2.8  First deploy → capture `FRONTEND_URL` (NV but returns fixed `https://hoa-example-org.vercel.app` until DNS).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. **CMS / API (Strapi)**\\\\\\\\n3.1  `npx create-strapi-app@latest hoa-cms` (v4, TypeScript).  \\\\\\\\n3.2  Install plugins: `npm i strapi-provider-upload-aws-s3 strapi-plugin-users-permissions strapi-plugin-audit-log`.  \\\\\\\\n3.3  Add `./config/middleware.js` JWT validation using Auth0 JWKS:  \\\\\\\\n```js\\\\\\\\nmodule.exports = [\\\\\\\\n  'strapi::errors',\\\\\\\\n  {\\\\\\\\n    name: 'global::auth0',\\\\\\\\n    config: { jwksUri: `https://${TENANT_ID}.us.auth0.com/.well-known/jwks.json` }\\\\\\\\n  },\\\\\\\\n  'strapi::security',\\\\\\\\n  'strapi::cors',\\\\\\\\n];\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n3.4  Implement route `/docs/signed-url` to issue S3 signed URLs after verifying Auth0 token roles.  \\\\\\\\n3.5  Commit & push to GitHub.\\\\\\\\n3.6  Render Blueprint deploy  \\\\\\\\n     – Web Service `hoa-cms` (Node 18).  \\\\\\\\n     – Env vars:  \\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nDATABASE_URL= (Render Postgres) (NV)\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_AUDIENCE=https://${TENANT_ID}.us.auth0.com/api/v2/\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_DOMAIN=${TENANT_ID}.us.auth0.com\\\\\\\\nS3_BUCKET=hoa-files\\\\\\\\nAWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=(V)\\\\\\\\nAWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=(V)\\\\\\\\nCORS_ORIGIN=https://hoa.example.org\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n     – Record `RENDER_SERVICE_ID` (V) and `API_URL=https://api.hoa-example-org.onrender.com` (NV).  \\\\\\\\n3.7  After first deploy, visit `/admin` to create Super Admin user (manual).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. **Storage / CDN**\\\\\\\\n4.1  `aws s3 mb s3://hoa-files` (V).  \\\\\\\\n4.2  `aws cloudfront create-distribution --origin-domain-name hoa-files.s3.amazonaws.com`  \\\\\\\\n     – Capture `CF_DIST_ID` & domain (V).  \\\\\\\\n4.3  IAM user `hoa-strapi-upload` w policy `PutObject/GetObject` on bucket; export keys above.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. **CI/CD Workflows**\\\\\\\\n5.1  In `hoa-site`: `.github/workflows/vercel.yml` running `vc deploy --prod`.  \\\\\\\\n5.2  In `hoa-cms`: `.github/workflows/render.yml` using Render deploy hook.  \\\\\\\\n5.3  Store `VERCEL_TOKEN`, `RENDER_TOKEN` secrets in GitHub (V).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. **Monitoring & Logging**\\\\\\\\n6.1  Add `/api/healthz` endpoints in both apps.  \\\\\\\\n6.2  Register both URLs in UptimeRobot.  \\\\\\\\n6.3  Add Sentry DSNs in env files (NV: SENTRY_DSN_FRONTEND / BACKEND).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. **DNS / SSL**\\\\\\\\n7.1  Create records in Route 53 (or registrar):  \\\\\\\\n     – `hoa.example.org` → CNAME `cname.vercel-dns.com.`  \\\\\\\\n     – `api.hoa.example.org` → A/ANAME Render IP.  \\\\\\\\n7.2  Add CNAME `cdn.hoa.example.org` → CloudFront domain.  \\\\\\\\n7.3  Update Strapi `settings` → `MEDIA_CDN_URL=https://cdn.hoa.example.org`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n8. **Smoke & Integration Tests**\\\\\\\\n8.1  `curl -I https://hoa.example.org | grep 200`.  \\\\\\\\n8.2  Obtain Auth0 test token → `curl -H \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" https://api.hoa.example.org/docs/signed-url` expect 200 JSON.  \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n9. **Admin Training & Handover**\\\\\\\\n9.1  Provide 5-min Loom video on posting an announcement and uploading a document.  \\\\\\\\n9.2  Deliver credentials vault entry to board secretary.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 5. Variable Outputs Summary\\\\\\\\n`TENANT_ID`, `CLIENT_ID`, `CLIENT_SECRET`, `M2M_CLIENT_ID`, `M2M_CLIENT_SECRET`, `AUTH0_SECRET`, `VERCEL_PROJECT_ID`, `FRONTEND_URL`, `DATABASE_URL`, `RENDER_SERVICE_ID`, `API_URL`, `S3_BUCKET`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID/SECRET`, `CF_DIST_ID`, `VERCEL_TOKEN`, `RENDER_TOKEN`, `SENTRY_DSN_*`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAll remaining commands are fully deterministic given these values.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n–– End of Unified Architecture DEP ––\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_auth_sync\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order auth-sync-v2 from agent 4: Refined DEP – Auth0 × Next.js × Strapi (Vercel / Render)\\\\\\\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nA. Auth0 Tenant Configuration\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Tenant\\\\\\\\n   • Name    : hoa-portal (prod), hoa-portal-dev (dev)\\\\\\\\n   • Auth0 Domain           : hoa-portal.us.auth0.com  (or custom CNAME login.hoa.com via Auth0 Custom Domains)\\\\\\\\n   • Default Alg.          : RS256\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. Applications\\\\\\\\n   2.1 Frontend (Next.js)\\\\\\\\n       • App Name        : hoa-portal-frontend\\\\\\\\n       • Type           : Single-Page Application (SPA)\\\\\\\\n       • Allowed Callback URLs\\\\\\\\n         ‣ PROD  https://hoa.vercel.app/api/auth/callback/auth0\\\\\\\\n         ‣ DEV   http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/auth0\\\\\\\\n       • Allowed Logout URLs\\\\\\\\n         ‣ https://hoa.vercel.app/\\\\\\\\n         ‣ http://localhost:3000/\\\\\\\\n       • Allowed Web Origins/CORS: same as hostnames above\\\\\\\\n       • Grant Types    : authorization_code, refresh_token, implicit (pkce)\\\\\\\\n   2.2 Backend / Strapi Management\\\\\\\\n       • App Name        : hoa-portal-strapi-s2s\\\\\\\\n       • Type           : Machine-to-Machine (M2M)\\\\\\\\n       • Allowed Token Audiences : Auth0 Management API & hoa-portal-api (see §3)\\\\\\\\n       • Usage          : Strapi CRON / Admin jobs that need Management API (optional)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. API / Resource Server (JWT audience)\\\\\\\\n   • Name      : hoa-portal-api\\\\\\\\n   • Identifier: https://api.hoa-portal.com     (<aud> in JWT)\\\\\\\\n   • Scopes    : read:docs  write:docs  admin:all\\\\\\\\n   • RBAC      : Enable \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"RBAC\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" & \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Add Permissions in Access Tokens\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" toggles.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Roles & Permissions Mapping\\\\\\\\n   ┌───────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┐\\\\\\\\n   │ Role      │ Permissions (Auth0 API scopes)           │\\\\\\\\n   ├───────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤\\\\\\\\n   │ resident  │ read:docs                                │\\\\\\\\n   │ admin     │ read:docs • write:docs • admin:all       │\\\\\\\\n   └───────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────┘\\\\\\\\n   • Role assignment stored in user.app_metadata → roles[] ; used by Strapi policy.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nB. Next.js (Vercel) – NextAuth Integration\\\\\\\\n──────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Packages    : next-auth @next-auth/auth0-provider jsonwebtoken jwks-rsa\\\\\\\\n2. ENV (Vercel)\\\\\\\\n   AUTH0_CLIENT_ID            = <hoa-portal-frontend Client ID>\\\\\\\\n   AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET        = <Secret>\\\\\\\\n   AUTH0_ISSUER_BASE_URL      = https://hoa-portal.us.auth0.com\\\\\\\\n   AUTH0_SCOPE                = openid profile email offline_access\\\\\\\\n   NEXTAUTH_URL               = https://hoa.vercel.app (or http://localhost:3000)\\\\\\\\n   NEXTAUTH_SECRET            = rand_32B\\\\\\\\n3. [...nextauth].ts\\\\\\\\n   import Auth0Provider from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"next-auth/providers/auth0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\n   export default NextAuth({\\\\\\\\n     providers: [Auth0Provider({\\\\\\\\n       clientId: process.env.AUTH0_CLIENT_ID,\\\\\\\\n       clientSecret: process.env.AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET,\\\\\\\\n       issuer: process.env.AUTH0_ISSUER_BASE_URL,\\\\\\\\n       authorization: { params: { audience: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://api.hoa-portal.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" } },\\\\\\\\n     })],\\\\\\\\n     callbacks: {\\\\\\\\n       async jwt({ token, account }) {\\\\\\\\n         if (account?.access_token) token.accessToken = account.access_token;\\\\\\\\n         return token;\\\\\\\\n       },\\\\\\\\n       async session({ session, token }) {\\\\\\\\n         session.accessToken = token.accessToken;\\\\\\\\n         return session;\\\\\\\\n       },\\\\\\\\n     },\\\\\\\\n   });\\\\\\\\n4. Protected Pages: use getServerSession() or useSession() w/ role checks.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nC. Strapi (Render) – JWT Validation Middleware\\\\\\\\n───────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Install\\\\\\\\n   yarn add jwks-rsa jsonwebtoken\\\\\\\\n2. ./src/middlewares/auth0.js\\\\\\\\n   const jwksRsa = require(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"jwks-rsa\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\");\\\\\\\\n   const jwt = require(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"jsonwebtoken\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\");\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   module.exports = (config, { strapi }) => {\\\\\\\\n     const jwks = jwksRsa.expressJwtSecret({\\\\\\\\n       cache: true,\\\\\\\\n       rateLimit: true,\\\\\\\\n       jwksRequestsPerMinute: 5,\\\\\\\\n       jwksUri: `https://hoa-portal.us.auth0.com/.well-known/jwks.json`,\\\\\\\\n     });\\\\\\\\n     return async (ctx, next) => {\\\\\\\\n       const token = ctx.request.header.authorization?.split(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")[1];\\\\\\\\n       if (!token) return ctx.unauthorized(`No auth token`);\\\\\\\\n       try {\\\\\\\\n         const decoded = jwt.verify(token, jwks, {\\\\\\\\n           audience: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://api.hoa-portal.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n           issuer: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://hoa-portal.us.auth0.com/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n           algorithms: [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"RS256\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\n         });\\\\\\\\n         ctx.state.user = decoded;\\\\\\\\n       } catch (err) {\\\\\\\\n         return ctx.unauthorized(`Invalid token`);\\\\\\\\n       }\\\\\\\\n       await next();\\\\\\\\n     };\\\\\\\\n   };\\\\\\\\n3. Enable in ./config/middleware.js (before router)\\\\\\\\n4. Role Enforcement Policy\\\\\\\\n   ./src/policies/require-scope.js → checks ctx.state.user[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"].includes(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"read:docs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") etc.\\\\\\\\n   Apply per-route in routes config.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD. Secure Document Access – Presigned S3 URLs\\\\\\\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Storage Layout\\\\\\\\n   s3://hoa-docs/prod/\\\\\\\\n         ├─ public/        (# public to residents)\\\\\\\\n         └─ admin-only/    (# financials, minutes)\\\\\\\\n2. Strapi Endpoint GET /docs/:id\\\\\\\\n   • Middleware validates JWT & scope.\\\\\\\\n   • Strapi queries doc metadata (path, classification).\\\\\\\\n   • Access Matrix\\\\\\\\n       resident → public/* only\\\\\\\\n       admin    → both prefixes\\\\\\\\n   • generatePresignedUrl({ Bucket, Key, Expires: 600 });\\\\\\\\n   • Return { url, expiresAt }\\\\\\\\n3. S3 Bucket Policy\\\\\\\\n   • Block Public ACLs & Block Public Access.\\\\\\\\n   • IAM role for Strapi (Render deploy) with s3:GetObject permission on prefix prod/*.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nE. Revised Deterministic Execution Steps (supersedes §7)\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n01  Create Auth0 tenant & custom domain                      (DevOps)\\\\\\\\n02  Register apps/roles/scopes exactly as §A.2-4             (DevOps)\\\\\\\\n03  Populate resident users via Auth0 Mgmt API CSV import    (Admin)\\\\\\\\n04  Next.js: install packages & configure NextAuth (§B)      (Frontend)\\\\\\\\n05  Strapi: add auth0 middleware & policy (§C)               (Backend)\\\\\\\\n06  Implement S3 presigned URL service (§D)                  (Backend)\\\\\\\\n07  Update CI secrets on Vercel & Render                     (DevOps)\\\\\\\\n08  End-to-End test: login → fetch doc as resident/admin     (QA)\\\\\\\\n09  Enable MFA (tenant setting) for admin role only          (SecOps)\\\\\\\\n10  Promote to production after pen-test pass                (Release)\\\\\\\\n   (All steps deterministic; tenant IDs & ARNs recorded in config repo.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nF. Dependencies\\\\\\\\n   • Vercel env vars for NextAuth (§B.2)\\\\\\\\n   • Render service env vars: AUTH0_AUDIENCE, AUTH0_DOMAIN (§C)\\\\\\\\n   • AWS creds (IAM role) for Strapi → S3 (§D)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nG. Removed Items\\\\\\\\n   • Keycloak fallback eliminated per directive.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nEnd of refined DEP.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_ui_sync\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order ui-sync-v2 from agent 3: UPDATED UI / UX & CMS PLAN  –  HOA-Style Website (Strapi-based)\\\\\\\\n=================================================================\\\\\\\\nSequence-ID: ui-sync-v2\\\\\\\\nPrepared for: Delta (Chief)\\\\\\\\nPrepared by: Valerius (Director)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. SITEMAP (UNCHANGED)\\\\\\\\n----------------------\\\\\\\\nPublic\\\\\\\\n  • Home (/)\\\\\\\\n  • Bylaws (/bylaws)\\\\\\\\n  • Local Schools (/schools)\\\\\\\\n  • News & Events – headlines only (/news)\\\\\\\\n  • Contact Us (/contact)\\\\\\\\n  • Login / Register (/login, /register)\\\\\\\\nResident-Only (Auth0 protected)\\\\\\\\n  • Dues & Payments (/dues)\\\\\\\\n  • Annual Meeting Docs (/annual-meetings)\\\\\\\\n  • News & Events – full article (/news/:slug)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE & NAVIGATION  (UNCHANGED)\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n• Responsive top bar → hamburger drawer ≤992 px.\\\\\\\\n• Authenticated drop-down: Dashboard → Dues | Meetings | Logout.\\\\\\\\n• Breadcrumbs & footer as before.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. STRAPI v4 CMS INTEGRATION\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------\\\\\\\\nA. Deployment & Access\\\\\\\\n   • Strapi v4 hosted on managed VPS / PaaS (Railway, Render) behind HTTPS (cms.example.com).\\\\\\\\n   • Built-in admin UI for editors, protected via Strapi Roles & Permissions → “Content Editor”.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nB. Content Types\\\\\\\\n   1. Article (collection)\\\\\\\\n      – title (string)\\\\\\\\n      – slug (UID)\\\\\\\\n      – summary (rich-text)\\\\\\\\n      – content (rich-text)\\\\\\\\n      – coverImage (media, single)\\\\\\\\n      – category (enum: News, Event)\\\\\\\\n      – isResidentOnly (boolean)\\\\\\\\n      – publishedAt (datetime)\\\\\\\\n   2. Bylaw (single type)\\\\\\\\n      – pdfFile (media, single)\\\\\\\\n      – lastUpdated (date)\\\\\\\\n   3. AnnualMeetingMinutes (collection)\\\\\\\\n      – year (integer)\\\\\\\\n      – pdfFile (media)\\\\\\\\n   4. School (collection)\\\\\\\\n      – name (string)\\\\\\\\n      – website (url)\\\\\\\\n      – gradeLevels (string)\\\\\\\\n   5. DuesConfig (single type)\\\\\\\\n      – StripePriceID (string)  // forward-looking\\\\\\\\n      – currentAmount (decimal)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nC. Media & Documents\\\\\\\\n   • Use Strapi’s Upload plugin backed by S3 bucket (or local in dev). URLs are returned in API.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD. API Access\\\\\\\\n   • Enable Strapi GraphQL plugin for flexible queries; REST endpoints also available.\\\\\\\\n   • Public role: can read Article where `isResidentOnly=false`, Bylaw, School, Contact form POST.\\\\\\\\n   • Authenticated role: granted read access to all Article, AnnualMeetingMinutes, DuesConfig.\\\\\\\\n   • Use Auth0 JWT validation in Strapi to map Auth0 users → “Authenticated” role (strapi-provider-auth0 or custom middleware).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. FRONT-END DATA FLOW\\\\\\\\n----------------------\\\\\\\\nNext.js (static + ISR) pulls data at build-time or via `getStaticProps` revalidated every X minutes:\\\\\\\\n  • `GET /articles?filters[isResidentOnly][$eq]=false&_sort=publishedAt:desc&_limit=5` for public list.\\\\\\\\n  • GraphQL query for full article by slug (runtime client fetch) – route guard checks Auth0 + `isResidentOnly` flag.\\\\\\\\nProtected pages:\\\\\\\\n  – Implement HOC `withAuth()` that uses Auth0 React SDK; while loading, show spinner; unauthenticated → `/login?redirect=…`.\\\\\\\\n  – After Auth0 login, access token with Strapi-accepted audience is fetched silently, then included as Bearer in GraphQL/REST calls for resident-only data.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. ACCESSIBILITY & RESPONSIVE  (UNCHANGED CORE POINTS)\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n• WCAG 2.1 AA, color contrast, ARIA labels, skip-nav, prefers-reduced-motion.\\\\\\\\n• Semantic HTML + Landmark roles, keyboard nav in drawer.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. UPDATED DEP-STYLE IMPLEMENTATION OUTLINE\\\\\\\\n-------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nPhase 0 – Repos & CI\\\\\\\\n  – mono repo: `web/` (Next.js, TS)  &  `cms/` (Strapi).\\\\\\\\n  – GitHub Actions builds: CMS docker image; Web static export (or SSR via Vercel).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 1 – Strapi Setup\\\\\\\\n  – Generate content types above.\\\\\\\\n  – Configure Auth0 provider; set roles & permissions.\\\\\\\\n  – Seed sample content & upload docs.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 2 – Core Web Shell\\\\\\\\n  – Nav bar, footer, route scaffolding.\\\\\\\\n  – Responsive design & Tailwind setup.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 3 – Public Pages Data Fetch\\\\\\\\n  – Home highlights, Bylaws PDF link, Schools list (GraphQL static).\\\\\\\\n  – News & Events list (public subset).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 4 – Auth0 Integration & Guards\\\\\\\\n  – Install `@auth0/auth0-react`; create `AuthProvider`.\\\\\\\\n  – Build `withAuth` HOC; secure `/dues`, `/annual-meetings`, article detail if `isResidentOnly`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 5 – Resident Features\\\\\\\\n  – Dues page: placeholder to call `/api/pay` (stripe) and fetch DuesConfig for amount.\\\\\\\\n  – Annual Meeting listing downloads from Strapi media URLs.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 6 – Incremental Static Regeneration & Revalidation\\\\\\\\n  – ISR for article list & details every 5 min; webhook from Strapi triggers revalidate API endpoint.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 7 – Accessibility & QA\\\\\\\\n  – axe-core audit, screen-reader testing, keyboard focus traps.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 8 – Production Deployment\\\\\\\\n  – CMS → Railway (Docker) + Postgres add-on + S3 for uploads.\\\\\\\\n  – Web → Vercel w/ ENV (`STRAPI_URL`, `AUTH0_DOMAIN`, `AUTH0_CLIENT_ID`, etc.).\\\\\\\\n  – Cloudfront / Vercel CDN handles docs & images via S3/Vercel asset pipeline.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDependencies / Hand-offs\\\\\\\\n• Auth Team delivers tenants, callback URLs, RBAC rules.\\\\\\\\n• DevOps provides Postgres, S3 creds, secure ENV injection.\\\\\\\\n• Payments team for Stripe endpoint.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEnd of Report.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_devops_sync\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order devops-sync-v2 from agent 2: **Re-Aligned DevOps, Hosting & DEP – Vercel + Render + AWS S3 (Staging / Prod)**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Hosting Summary\\\\\\\\n   • **Front-end** (Next.js): Vercel Hobby plan – zero cost, auto-SSL, GitHub integration, preview deployments, analytics.\\\\\\\\n   • **CMS / API**: Strapi on Render Web Service  \\\\\\\\n        – Prod: Starter instance (1 CPU, 2 GB) ‑ $7/mo  \\\\\\\\n        – Staging: Free instance (auto-sleep) ‑ $0  \\\\\\\\n   • **Database**: Render Managed Postgres  \\\\\\\\n        – Prod: Starter 1 GB ‑ $7/mo (daily backups, 7-day retention)  \\\\\\\\n        – Staging: Free Dev DB (sleeping) ‑ $0\\\\\\\\n   • **Docs / Assets**: AWS S3 (per-env buckets) + CloudFront optional later.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. CI/CD & Environment Segregation\\\\\\\\n   • **Git flow**: `main`→prod, `develop`→staging.  \\\\\\\\n   • Vercel Git integration auto-deploys both branches to matching domains:  \\\\\\\\n        – prod:  https://www.<domain>  \\\\\\\\n        – staging: https://staging.<domain>  \\\\\\\\n   • Render Blueprints watch GitHub; push to `develop` builds staging app; merge to `main` triggers prod build.\\\\\\\\n   • GitHub Actions runs unified test suite (frontend + backend) before merge; status required.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Backups & DR\\\\\\\\n   • Render DB daily backups (included).  \\\\\\\\n   • **Weekly pg_dump → S3** via scheduled GitHub Action (`cron-backup.yml`) storing dumps in `/backups/YYYY-MM` folder, S3 lifecycle 30-day retention.  \\\\\\\\n   • S3 versioning + Cross-Region Replication toggle available for future.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Monitoring / Logging / Alerts\\\\\\\\n   • Vercel & Render provide real-time logs; export via `vercel logs` / `render logs`.  \\\\\\\\n   • **Sentry**: browser SDK in Next.js, Node SDK in Strapi; DSNs kept as secrets.  \\\\\\\\n   • **UptimeRobot** free plan pinging prod & staging every 5 min (HTTPS + keyword).  \\\\\\\\n   • Render health-checks + notification (>80% CPU, >512 MB swap) to Ops email.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. Security Hardening\\\\\\\\n   • Vercel / Render auto-TLS (Let’s Encrypt).  \\\\\\\\n   • GitHub Dependabot + Snyk OSS weekly scan.  \\\\\\\\n   • Render firewall: only 443 ingress; Postgres restricted to internal service network.  \\\\\\\\n   • AWS S3 bucket policy: private, HTTPS-only, IAM user with least-privilege PUT/GET for backups.\\\\\\\\n   • Enforce MFA: GitHub, AWS IAM, Render, Vercel.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. Secrets Management\\\\\\\\n   • **GitHub** → environment secrets (SENTRY_DSN, AWS creds for backup workflow).  \\\\\\\\n   • **Render** → encrypted env vars (JWT_SECRET, DB_URL, AWS_S3_BUCKET, SMTP).  \\\\\\\\n   • **Vercel** → Environment Variables per env (API_URL, SENTRY_DSN_FRONTEND).  \\\\\\\\n   • No secrets committed; GitHub OIDC to AWS removes static keys (optional advanced step).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. Recurring Cost Estimate (Monthly)\\\\\\\\n   • Render Strapi (Starter prod) …………………  $7\\\\\\\\n   • Render Postgres (Starter prod) ……………  $7\\\\\\\\n   • Render staging tiers ………………………………  $0  (free & sleeping)\\\\\\\\n   • Vercel Hobby (≤100 GB bandwidth) ………  $0\\\\\\\\n   • AWS S3 10 GB @ $0.023/GB …………………  $0.25\\\\\\\\n   • UptimeRobot / Sentry free tiers …………   $0\\\\\\\\n   ––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––\\\\\\\\n   • **Total ≈ $14.25 / month**  (headroom to $35 budget)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n8. Deterministic Executable Plan (DEP)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-0  – Local Prereqs\\\\\\\\n  brew install terraform awscli vercel-cli render\\\\\\\\n  export ORG=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hoa\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"  # used as name prefix\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-1  – Clone Infra Repo\\\\\\\\n  git clone git@github.com:<org>/hoa-infra.git && cd hoa-infra\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-2  – AWS S3 via Terraform (per env)\\\\\\\\n  # modules/s3.tf\\\\\\\\n  terraform init\\\\\\\\n  for ENV in staging prod; do\\\\\\\\n    terraform workspace select $ENV || terraform workspace new $ENV\\\\\\\\n    terraform apply -var=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"env=$ENV\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -auto-approve  # creates: s3 bucket, IAM user+policy\\\\\\\\n  done\\\\\\\\n  # Outputs saved: S3_BUCKET_$ENV, AWS_ACCESS_KEY_$ENV, AWS_SECRET_KEY_$ENV\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-3  – Render Blueprints\\\\\\\\n  # files: strapi-staging.yaml, strapi-prod.yaml\\\\\\\\n  render blueprint apply -f strapi-staging.yaml\\\\\\\\n  render blueprint apply -f strapi-prod.yaml\\\\\\\\n  ## Blueprints include service type, branch, dockerfile path, env vars (placeholders)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-4  – Vercel Setup (CLI)\\\\\\\\n  vercel login  # browser auth\\\\\\\\n  vercel link   # in frontend repo\\\\\\\\n  vercel project env add API_URL https://strapi-$ENV.onrender.com --env $ENV\\\\\\\\n  vercel project env add SENTRY_DSN_FRONTEND $SENTRY_DSN --env $ENV\\\\\\\\n  vercel env pull .env.local --yes  # sync local\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-5  – GitHub Secrets / Variables\\\\\\\\n  gh secret set AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID_STG  <output AWS_ACCESS_KEY_staging>\\\\\\\\n  gh secret set AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_STG  <output AWS_SECRET_KEY_staging>\\\\\\\\n  gh secret set AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID_PROD <output AWS_ACCESS_KEY_prod>\\\\\\\\n  gh secret set AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_PROD <output AWS_SECRET_KEY_prod>\\\\\\\\n  gh secret set SENTRY_DSN             $SENTRY_DSN_BACK\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-6  – CI / GitHub Actions\\\\\\\\n  # .github/workflows/ci.yml (lint+unit tests)\\\\\\\\n  # .github/workflows/cron-backup.yml (weekly pg_dump → S3)\\\\\\\\n  git add .github && git commit -m \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ci & backup pipelines\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" && git push\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-7  – Domain & SSL (if custom domain)\\\\\\\\n  vercel domains add www.<domain>\\\\\\\\n  render custom-domain add strapi-prod <api.<domain>>\\\\\\\\n  # ACME challenge automated by providers\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-8  – Monitoring\\\\\\\\n  curl -X POST https://uptimerobot.com/api/ ...  # create monitors via API (script in infra/monitoring.sh)\\\\\\\\n  # Sentry DSNs already active via env vars.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-9  – Verification\\\\\\\\n  vercel --prod  # trigger production build\\\\\\\\n  render deploy strapi-prod\\\\\\\\n  curl https://www.<domain>/health   # expect 200 OK\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAll steps deterministic given valid tokens.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n9. Planning-Phase Deliverables\\\\\\\\n  • infra/terraform/ (S3 & IAM module)\\\\\\\\n  • render/strapi-*.yaml  (blueprint files)\\\\\\\\n  • .github/workflows/{ci.yml,cron-backup.yml}\\\\\\\\n  • docs/monitoring.sh (optional helper)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nReady to proceed to Execution when approved.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-26T18:47:08.656Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###phaseExec1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"All Director-rank agents have delivered harmonized, domain-specific DEPs. I have merged these into a single, end-to-end Deterministically Executable Plan that installs the complete HOA website using Vercel (Next.js), Render (Strapi + Postgres), Auth0, and AWS S3. The plan enumerates every step, flags all non-deterministic outputs for capture, and clearly defines inter-module dependencies. We are ready to shift from Planning to Execution.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"MASTER DEP – HOA WEBSITE (Vercel / Render / Auth0 / AWS S3)\\\\nSymbols: (V)=value captured deterministically; (NV)=provider-generated value recorded for later use.\\\\nPrereqs: Local workstation w/ Node 18, yarn, git, awscli, vercel-cli, render, terraform, jq.\\\\n----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n0.  Repositories\\\\n    0.1  git clone git@github.com:<org>/hoa-site.git   (frontend)\\\\n    0.2  git clone git@github.com:<org>/hoa-cms.git    (backend)\\\\n    0.3  git clone git@github.com:<org>/hoa-infra.git  (infra)\\\\n\\\\n1.  Auth0 Tenant  (run once)\\\\n    1.1  auth0 tenants create hoa-portal-prod          → TENANT_ID  (NV)\\\\n    1.2  auth0 apps create spa hoa-next --callbacks https://hoa.example.org/api/auth/callback/auth0 --logout-urls https://hoa.example.org/ --type spa → CLIENT_ID/SECRET (V)\\\\n    1.3  auth0 apps create m2m hoa-strapi --audience https://api.hoa.example.org → M2M_CLIENT_ID/SECRET (V)\\\\n    1.4  auth0 apis create hoa-api --identifier https://api.hoa.example.org --signing-alg RS256\\\\n    1.5  auth0 roles create resident; auth0 roles create board; assign scopes read:docs (resident) / admin:all (board).\\\\n\\\\n2.  AWS S3 & IAM via Terraform (hoa-infra)\\\\n    2.1  terraform -chdir=terraform init\\\\n    2.2  for ENV in staging prod; do\\\\n           terraform workspace select $ENV || terraform workspace new $ENV\\\\n           terraform apply -var=\\\\\\\"env=$ENV\\\\\\\" -auto-approve   # creates bucket, IAM user\\\\n         done\\\\n         → S3_BUCKET_$ENV, AWS_ACCESS_KEY_$ENV, AWS_SECRET_KEY_$ENV (V)\\\\n\\\\n3.  Render Services (Strapi + Postgres)\\\\n    3.1  render blueprint apply -f render/strapi-staging.yaml   → RENDER_SERVICE_ID_STG (V)  (DB_URL_STG NV)\\\\n    3.2  render blueprint apply -f render/strapi-prod.yaml      → RENDER_SERVICE_ID_PROD (V)  (DB_URL_PROD NV)\\\\n\\\\n4.  Vercel Front-End\\\\n    4.1  cd hoa-site && vercel link                           → VERCEL_PROJECT_ID (V)\\\\n    4.2  vercel env add PROD  API_URL https://api.hoa.example.org\\\\n         vercel env add PROD  AUTH0_*  (values from step 1)\\\\n         vercel env add PROD  NEXTAUTH_SECRET $(openssl rand -hex 32)  (NV)\\\\n    4.3  vercel env add STAGING equivalents (api-staging URL)\\\\n\\\\n5.  Strapi Configuration\\\\n    5.1  cd hoa-cms\\\\n         yarn add strapi-provider-upload-aws-s3 jwks-rsa jsonwebtoken\\\\n    5.2  echo \\\\\\\"AUTH0_DOMAIN=${TENANT_ID}.us.auth0.com\\\\\\\" >> .env\\\\n         echo \\\\\\\"AWS_S3_BUCKET=$S3_BUCKET_prod\\\\\\\" >> .env\\\\n         # commit auth0 middleware (+ content types) – deterministic file set\\\\n    5.3  git commit -m \\\\\\\"feat: auth0 + s3 integration\\\\\\\" && git push\\\\n    5.4  Render auto-redeploy; verify https://api.hoa.example.org/admin (manual Super-Admin creation).\\\\n\\\\n6.  GitHub Secrets / CI\\\\n    6.1  gh secret set VERCEL_TOKEN              # personal token (NV)\\\\n    6.2  gh secret set RENDER_TOKEN              # personal token (NV)\\\\n    6.3  gh secret set AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID_STG     $AWS_ACCESS_KEY_staging\\\\n    6.4  gh secret set AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_STG $AWS_SECRET_KEY_staging\\\\n    6.5  gh secret set AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID_PROD    $AWS_ACCESS_KEY_prod\\\\n    6.6  gh secret set AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_PROD $AWS_SECRET_KEY_prod\\\\n    6.7  Push .github/workflows/{vercel.yml,render.yml,backup.yml}\\\\n\\\\n7.  DNS & SSL\\\\n    7.1  Route 53 records:\\\\n         hoa.example.org  → CNAME cname.vercel-dns.com.       (front-end)\\\\n         api.hoa.example.org → A record Render IP.\\\\n    7.2  CloudFront distribution (optional public docs) → CNAME cdn.hoa.example.org → update Strapi `MEDIA_CDN_URL`.\\\\n\\\\n8.  Monitoring & Alerts\\\\n    8.1  curl -XPOST https://uptimerobot.com/api/newMonitor … for\\\\n         – https://hoa.example.org/healthz\\\\n         – https://api.hoa.example.org/healthz\\\\n    8.2  Sentry: set DSN env vars in Vercel & Render.\\\\n\\\\n9.  Smoke Tests (deterministic)\\\\n    9.1  curl -I https://hoa.example.org | grep \\\\\\\"200\\\\\\\"\\\\n    9.2  TOKEN=$(auth0 test-token …resident…) &&\\\\n         curl -H \\\\\\\"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\\\\\\\" https://api.hoa.example.org/docs/signed-url | jq -e .url\\\\n\\\\n10. Admin Training & Handoff\\\\n     10.1  Record 5-min Loom demonstrating Strapi post & file upload.\\\\n     10.2  Deliver 1Password vault entry with Auth0, Vercel, Render credentials.\\\\n----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nVARIABLE OUTPUTS SUMMARY\\\\nTENANT_ID, CLIENT_ID/SECRET, M2M_CLIENT_ID/SECRET, VERCEL_PROJECT_ID, NEXTAUTH_SECRET, S3_BUCKET_{staging,prod}, AWS_ACCESS/SECRET KEYS, RENDER_SERVICE_ID_{STG,PROD}, DB_URL_{STG,PROD}, VERCEL_TOKEN, RENDER_TOKEN, SENTRY_DSN_FRONT/BACK.\\\\nAll subsequent CLI steps are deterministic once these values are set.\\\"\\n}\\n###phaseExec1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-26T18:48:51.117Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"phaseExec1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DENIED_BY_INTERNAL_REVIEW\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Phase shift was denied by internal review. Feedback from Partagaz D:\\\\\\\\nDENY\\\\\\\\nThe DEP is denied for the following reasons:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.  **Undefined User Require