\\\n• **File Storage** – AWS S3 bucket (`hoa-files`)  \\\\\\\\n  – Prefix `/public` (world-read) fronted by CloudFront.  \\\\\\\\n  – Prefix `/private` requires time-limited signed URLs generated by Strapi.  \\\\\\\\n• **CI/CD** – GitHub Actions → Vercel & Render.  \\\\\\\\n• **Monitoring** – UptimeRobot + Sentry.  \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 2. Key Modules / Services\\\\\\\\n1. **Public Website** (Next.js) – Home, About, Contact, Amenities.  \\\\\\\\n2. **Resident Portal** (Next.js SSR) – Dashboard, profile, announcements, documents.  \\\\\\\\n3. **CMS / API** (Strapi) – Content types, media library, role-based permissions.  \\\\\\\\n4. **Auth Layer** – Auth0 tenant, SPA + M2M applications, JWKS endpoint, RBAC roles: `resident`, `board`.  \\\\\\\\n5. **Storage** – S3 + CloudFront; signed URL service in Strapi `/docs/signed-url`.  \\\\\\\\n6. **CI/CD & Monitoring** – GitHub Actions workflows, Sentry SDKs, UptimeRobot.  \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 3. Cross-Director Integrations\\\\\\\\n• DNS/Email Director – Domain records, Postmark SMTP creds for Auth0 email + Strapi reset.  \\\\\\\\n• Security/Compliance Director – Review Auth0 tenant config, S3 IAM policy, JWT expiry.  \\\\\\\\n• Payments Director (optional) – Stripe keys if dues payment added later.  \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 4. Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)\\\\\\\\n`(V)` = deterministic value captured, reuse later `(NV)` = non-deterministic generated value noted.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n0. **Prerequisites**  \\\\\\\\n   Repo `hoa-site` (front-end) and `hoa-cms` (back-end) exist in GitHub org.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **Auth0 Tenant Setup**\\\\\\\\n1.1  Create tenant `hoa-prod` (NV: TENANT_ID).  \\\\\\\\n1.2  Create **SPA Application** `hoa-next`  \\\\\\\\n     – Callback URL `https://hoa.example.org/api/auth/callback/auth0`  \\\\\\\\n     – Allowed Logout URL `https://hoa.example.org/`  \\\\\\\\n     – Capture `CLIENT_ID`, `CLIENT_SECRET` (V).  \\\\\\\\n1.3  Create **M2M Application** `hoa-strapi`  \\\\\\\\n     – Authorize to Management API `read:users`  \\\\\\\\n     – Capture `M2M_CLIENT_ID`, `M2M_CLIENT_SECRET` (V).  \\\\\\\\n1.4  Define roles `resident`, `board` in Auth0 RBAC. (deterministic).  \\\\\\\\n1.5  Enable RBAC & add custom claim `https://hoa/roles` in tokens.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. **Front-End (Next.js)**\\\\\\\\n2.1  `npx create-next-app@latest hoa-site --typescript`.  \\\\\\\\n2.2  Add Auth0 SDK: `npm i @auth0/nextjs-auth0`.  \\\\\\\\n2.3  Configure `.env.local`  \\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_SECRET=(NV openssl rand -hex 32)\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_BASE_URL=https://hoa.example.org\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_ISSUER_BASE_URL=https://${TENANT_ID}.us.auth0.com\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_CLIENT_ID=${CLIENT_ID}\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET=${CLIENT_SECRET}\\\\\\\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.hoa.example.org\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n2.4  Implement API proxy route `/api/token` to exchange and silently refresh tokens for Strapi calls.  \\\\\\\\n2.5  Protect resident pages with `withPageAuthRequired` HOC.\\\\\\\\n2.6  Commit & push to GitHub.  \\\\\\\\n2.7  Vercel import repo → project `hoa-site`  \\\\\\\\n     – Record `VERCEL_PROJECT_ID` (V).  \\\\\\\\n     – Set env vars from step 2.3.  \\\\\\\\n2.8  First deploy → capture `FRONTEND_URL` (NV but returns fixed `https://hoa-example-org.vercel.app` until DNS).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. **CMS / API (Strapi)**\\\\\\\\n3.1  `npx create-strapi-app@latest hoa-cms` (v4, TypeScript).  \\\\\\\\n3.2  Install plugins: `npm i strapi-provider-upload-aws-s3 strapi-plugin-users-permissions strapi-plugin-audit-log`.  \\\\\\\\n3.3  Add `./config/middleware.js` JWT validation using Auth0 JWKS:  \\\\\\\\n```js\\\\\\\\nmodule.exports = [\\\\\\\\n  'strapi::errors',\\\\\\\\n  {\\\\\\\\n    name: 'global::auth0',\\\\\\\\n    config: { jwksUri: `https://${TENANT_ID}.us.auth0.com/.well-known/jwks.json` }\\\\\\\\n  },\\\\\\\\n  'strapi::security',\\\\\\\\n  'strapi::cors',\\\\\\\\n];\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n3.4  Implement route `/docs/signed-url` to issue S3 signed URLs after verifying Auth0 token roles.  \\\\\\\\n3.5  Commit & push to GitHub.\\\\\\\\n3.6  Render Blueprint deploy  \\\\\\\\n     – Web Service `hoa-cms` (Node 18).  \\\\\\\\n     – Env vars:  \\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nDATABASE_URL= (Render Postgres) (NV)\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_AUDIENCE=https://${TENANT_ID}.us.auth0.com/api/v2/\\\\\\\\nAUTH0_DOMAIN=${TENANT_ID}.us.auth0.com\\\\\\\\nS3_BUCKET=hoa-files\\\\\\\\nAWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=(V)\\\\\\\\nAWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=(V)\\\\\\\\nCORS_ORIGIN=https://hoa.example.org\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n     – Record `RENDER_SERVICE_ID` (V) and `API_URL=https://api.hoa-example-org.onrender.com` (NV).  \\\\\\\\n3.7  After first deploy, visit `/admin` to create Super Admin user (manual).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. **Storage / CDN**\\\\\\\\n4.1  `aws s3 mb s3://hoa-files` (V).  \\\\\\\\n4.2  `aws cloudfront create-distribution --origin-domain-name hoa-files.s3.amazonaws.com`  \\\\\\\\n     – Capture `CF_DIST_ID` & domain (V).  \\\\\\\\n4.3  IAM user `hoa-strapi-upload` w policy `PutObject/GetObject` on bucket; export keys above.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. **CI/CD Workflows**\\\\\\\\n5.1  In `hoa-site`: `.github/workflows/vercel.yml` running `vc deploy --prod`.  \\\\\\\\n5.2  In `hoa-cms`: `.github/workflows/render.yml` using Render deploy hook.  \\\\\\\\n5.3  Store `VERCEL_TOKEN`, `RENDER_TOKEN` secrets in GitHub (V).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. **Monitoring & Logging**\\\\\\\\n6.1  Add `/api/healthz` endpoints in both apps.  \\\\\\\\n6.2  Register both URLs in UptimeRobot.  \\\\\\\\n6.3  Add Sentry DSNs in env files (NV: SENTRY_DSN_FRONTEND / BACKEND).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. **DNS / SSL**\\\\\\\\n7.1  Create records in Route 53 (or registrar):  \\\\\\\\n     – `hoa.example.org` → CNAME `cname.vercel-dns.com.`  \\\\\\\\n     – `api.hoa.example.org` → A/ANAME Render IP.  \\\\\\\\n7.2  Add CNAME `cdn.hoa.example.org` → CloudFront domain.  \\\\\\\\n7.3  Update Strapi `settings` → `MEDIA_CDN_URL=https://cdn.hoa.example.org`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n8. **Smoke & Integration Tests**\\\\\\\\n8.1  `curl -I https://hoa.example.org | grep 200