\\\\\\\n         ‣ http://localhost:3000/\\\\\\\\n       • Allowed Web Origins/CORS: same as hostnames above\\\\\\\\n       • Grant Types    : authorization_code, refresh_token, implicit (pkce)\\\\\\\\n   2.2 Backend / Strapi Management\\\\\\\\n       • App Name        : hoa-portal-strapi-s2s\\\\\\\\n       • Type           : Machine-to-Machine (M2M)\\\\\\\\n       • Allowed Token Audiences : Auth0 Management API & hoa-portal-api (see §3)\\\\\\\\n       • Usage          : Strapi CRON / Admin jobs that need Management API (optional)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. API / Resource Server (JWT audience)\\\\\\\\n   • Name      : hoa-portal-api\\\\\\\\n   • Identifier: https://api.hoa-portal.com     (<aud> in JWT)\\\\\\\\n   • Scopes    : read:docs  write:docs  admin:all\\\\\\\\n   • RBAC      : Enable \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"RBAC\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" & \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Add Permissions in Access Tokens\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" toggles.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Roles & Permissions Mapping\\\\\\\\n   ┌───────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┐\\\\\\\\n   │ Role      │ Permissions (Auth0 API scopes)           │\\\\\\\\n   ├───────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤\\\\\\\\n   │ resident  │ read:docs                                │\\\\\\\\n   │ admin     │ read:docs • write:docs • admin:all       │\\\\\\\\n   └───────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────┘\\\\\\\\n   • Role assignment stored in user.app_metadata → roles[] ; used by Strapi policy.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nB. Next.js (Vercel) – NextAuth Integration\\\\\\\\n──────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Packages    : next-auth @next-auth/auth0-provider jsonwebtoken jwks-rsa\\\\\\\\n2. ENV (Vercel)\\\\\\\\n   AUTH0_CLIENT_ID            = <hoa-portal-frontend Client ID>\\\\\\\\n   AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET        = <Secret>\\\\\\\\n   AUTH0_ISSUER_BASE_URL      = https://hoa-portal.us.auth0.com\\\\\\\\n   AUTH0_SCOPE                = openid profile email offline_access\\\\\\\\n   NEXTAUTH_URL               = https://hoa.vercel.app (or http://localhost:3000)\\\\\\\\n   NEXTAUTH_SECRET            = rand_32B\\\\\\\\n3. [...nextauth].ts\\\\\\\\n   import Auth0Provider from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"next-auth/providers/auth0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\n   export default NextAuth({\\\\\\\\n     providers: [Auth0Provider({\\\\\\\\n       clientId: process.env.AUTH0_CLIENT_ID,\\\\\\\\n       clientSecret: process.env.AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET,\\\\\\\\n       issuer: process.env.AUTH0_ISSUER_BASE_URL,\\\\\\\\n       authorization: { params: { audience: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://api.hoa-portal.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" } },\\\\\\\\n     })],\\\\\\\\n     callbacks: {\\\\\\\\n       async jwt({ token, account }) {\\\\\\\\n         if (account?.access_token) token.accessToken = account.access_token;\\\\\\\\n         return token;\\\\\\\\n       },\\\\\\\\n       async session({ session, token }) {\\\\\\\\n         session.accessToken = token.accessToken;\\\\\\\\n         return session;\\\\\\\\n       },\\\\\\\\n     },\\\\\\\\n   });\\\\\\\\n4. Protected Pages: use getServerSession() or useSession() w/ role checks.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nC. Strapi (Render) – JWT Validation Middleware\\\\\\\\n───────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Install\\\\\\\\n   yarn add jwks-rsa jsonwebtoken\\\\\\\\n2. ./src/middlewares/auth0.js\\\\\\\\n   const jwksRsa = require(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"jwks-rsa\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\");\\\\\\\\n   const jwt = require(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"jsonwebtoken\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\");\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   module.exports = (config, { strapi }) => {\\\\\\\\n     const jwks = jwksRsa.expressJwtSecret({\\\\\\\\n       cache: true,\\\\\\\\n       rateLimit: true,\\\\\\\\n       jwksRequestsPerMinute: 5,\\\\\\\\n       jwksUri: `https://hoa-portal.us.auth0.com/.well-known/jwks.json`,\\\\\\\\n     });\\\\\\\\n     return async (ctx, next) => {\\\\\\\\n       const token = ctx.request.header.authorization?.split(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")[1];\\\\\\\\n       if (!token) return ctx.unauthorized(`No auth token`);\\\\\\\\n       try {\\\\\\\\n         const decoded = jwt.verify(token, jwks, {\\\\\\\\n           audience: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://api.hoa-portal.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n           issuer: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://hoa-portal.us.auth0.com/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n           algorithms: [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"RS256\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\n         });\\\\\\\\n         ctx.state.user = decoded;\\\\\\\\n       } catch (err) {\\\\\\\\n         return ctx.unauthorized(`Invalid token`);\\\\\\\\n       }\\\\\\\\n       await next();\\\\\\\\n     };\\\\\\\\n   };\\\\\\\\n3. Enable in ./config/middleware.js (before router)\\\\\\\\n4. Role Enforcement Policy\\\\\\\\n   ./src/policies/require-scope.js → checks ctx.state.user[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"].includes(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"read:docs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") etc.\\\\\\\\n   Apply per-route in routes config.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD. Secure Document Access – Presigned S3 URLs\\\\\\\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Storage Layout\\\\\\\\n   s3://hoa-docs/prod/\\\\\\\\n         ├─ public/        (# public to residents)\\\\\\\\n         └─ admin-only/    (# financials, minutes)\\\\\\\\n2. Strapi Endpoint GET /docs/:id\\\\\\\\n   • Middleware validates JWT & scope.\\\\\\\\n   • Strapi queries doc metadata (path, classification).\\\\\\\\n   • Access Matrix\\\\\\\\n       resident → public/* only\\\\\\\\n       admin    → both prefixes\\\\\\\\n   • generatePresignedUrl({ Bucket, Key, Expires: 600 });\\\\\\\\n   • Return { url, expiresAt }\\\\\\\\n3. S3 Bucket Policy\\\\\\\\n   • Block Public ACLs & Block Public Access.\\\\\\\\n   • IAM role for Strapi (Render deploy) with s3:GetObject permission on prefix prod/*.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nE. Revised Deterministic Execution Steps (supersedes §7)\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n01  Create Auth0 tenant & custom domain                      (DevOps)\\\\\\\\n02  Register apps/roles/scopes exactly as §A.2-4             (DevOps)\\\\\\\\n03  Populate resident users via Auth0 Mgmt API CSV import    (Admin)\\\\\\\\n04  Next.js: install packages & configure NextAuth (§B)      (Frontend)\\\\\\\\n05  Strapi: add auth0 middleware & policy (§C)               (Backend)\\\\\\\\n06  Implement S3 presigned URL service (§D)                  (Backend)\\\\\\\\n07  Update CI secrets on Vercel & Render                     (DevOps)\\\\\\\\n08  End-to-End test: login → fetch doc as resident/admin     (QA)\\\\\\\\n09  Enable MFA (tenant setting) for admin role only          (SecOps)\\\\\\\\n10  Promote to production after pen-test pass                (Release)\\\\\\\\n   (All steps deterministic; tenant IDs & ARNs recorded in config repo.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nF. Dependencies\\\\\\\\n   • Vercel env vars for NextAuth (§B.2)\\\\\\\\n   • Render service env vars: AUTH0_AUDIENCE, AUTH0_DOMAIN (§C)\\\\\\\\n   • AWS creds (IAM role) for Strapi → S3 (§D)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nG. Removed Items\\\\\\\\n   • Keycloak fallback eliminated per directive.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nEnd of refined DEP.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_ui_sync\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order ui-sync-v2 from agent 3: UPDATED UI / UX & CMS PLAN  –  HOA-Style Website (Strapi-based)\\\\\\\\n=================================================================\\\\\\\\nSequence-ID: ui-sync-v2\\\\\\\\nPrepared for: Delta (Chief)\\\\\\\\nPrepared by: Valerius (Director)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. SITEMAP (UNCHANGED)\\\\\\\\n----------------------\\\\\\\\nPublic\\\\\\\\n  • Home (/)\\\\\\\\n  • Bylaws (/bylaws)\\\\\\\\n  • Local Schools (/schools)\\\\\\\\n  • News & Events – headlines only (/news)\\\\\\\\n  • Contact Us (/contact)\\\\\\\\n  • Login / Register (/login, /register)\\\\\\\\nResident-Only (Auth0 protected)\\\\\\\\n  • Dues & Payments (/dues)\\\\\\\\n  • Annual Meeting Docs (/annual-meetings)\\\\\\\\n  • News & Events – full article (/news/:slug)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE & NAVIGATION  (UNCHANGED)\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n• Responsive top bar → hamburger drawer ≤992 px.\\\\\\\\n• Authenticated drop-down: Dashboard → Dues | Meetings | Logout.\\\\\\\\n• Breadcrumbs & footer as before.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. STRAPI v4 CMS INTEGRATION\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------\\\\\\\\nA. Deployment & Access\\\\\\\\n   • Strapi v4 hosted on managed VPS / PaaS (Railway, Render) behind HTTPS (cms.example.com).\\\\\\\\n   • Built-in admin UI for editors, protected via Strapi Roles & Permissions → “Content Editor”.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nB. Content Types\\\\\\\\n   1. Article (collection)\\\\\\\\n      – title (string)\\\\\\\\n      – slug (UID)\\\\\\\\n      – summary (rich-text)\\\\\\\\n      – content (rich-text)\\\\\\\\n      – coverImage (media, single)\\\\\\\\n      – category (enum: News, Event)\\\\\\\\n      – isResidentOnly (boolean)\\\\\\\\n      – publishedAt (datetime)\\\\\\\\n   2. Bylaw (single type)\\\\\\\\n      – pdfFile (media, single)\\\\\\\\n      – lastUpdated (date)\\\\\\\\n   3. AnnualMeetingMinutes (collection)\\\\\\\\n      – year (integer)\\\\\\\\n      – pdfFile (media)\\\\\\\\n   4. School (collection)\\\\\\\\n      – name (string)\\\\\\\\n      – website (url)\\\\\\\\n      – gradeLevels (string)\\\\\\\\n   5. DuesConfig (single type)\\\\\\\\n      – StripePriceID (string)  // forward-looking\\\\\\\\n      – currentAmount (decimal)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nC. Media & Documents\\\\\\\\n   • Use Strapi’s Upload plugin backed by S3 bucket (or local in dev). URLs are returned in API.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD. API Access\\\\\\\\n   • Enable Strapi GraphQL plugin for flexible queries; REST endpoints also available.\\\\\\\\n   • Public role: can read Article where `isResidentOnly=false`, Bylaw, School, Contact form POST.\\\\\\\\n   • Authenticated role: granted read access to all Article, AnnualMeetingMinutes, DuesConfig.\\\\\\\\n   • Use Auth0 JWT validation in Strapi to map Auth0 users → “Authenticated” role (strapi-provider-auth0 or custom middleware).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. FRONT-END DATA FLOW\\\\\\\\n----------------------\\\\\\\\nNext.js (static + ISR) pulls data at build-time or via `getStaticProps` revalidated every X minutes:\\\\\\\\n  • `GET /articles?filters[isResidentOnly][$eq]=false&_sort=publishedAt:desc&_limit=5` for public list.\\\\\\\\n  • GraphQL query for full article by slug (runtime client fetch) – route guard checks Auth0 + `isResidentOnly` flag.\\\\\\\\nProtected pages:\\\\\\\\n  – Implement HOC `withAuth()` that uses Auth0 React SDK; while loading, show spinner; unauthenticated → `/login?redirect=…`.\\\\\\\\n  – After Auth0 login, access token with Strapi-accepted audience is fetched silently, then included as Bearer in GraphQL/REST calls for resident-only data.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. ACCESSIBILITY & RESPONSIVE  (UNCHANGED CORE POINTS)\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n• WCAG 2.1 AA, color contrast, ARIA labels, skip-nav, prefers-reduced-motion.\\\\\\\\n• Semantic HTML + Landmark roles, keyboard nav in drawer.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. UPDATED DEP-STYLE IMPLEMENTATION OUTLINE\\\\\\\\n-------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nPhase 0 – Repos & CI\\\\\\\\n  – mono repo: `web/` (Next.js, TS)  &  `cms/` (Strapi).\\\\\\\\n  – GitHub Actions builds: CMS docker image; Web static export (or SSR via Vercel).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 1 – Strapi Setup\\\\\\\\n  – Generate content types above.\\\\\\\\n  – Configure Auth0 provider; set roles & permissions.\\\\\\\\n  – Seed sample content & upload docs.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 2 – Core Web Shell\\\\\\\\n  – Nav bar, footer, route scaffolding.\\\\\\\\n  – Responsive design & Tailwind setup.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 3 – Public Pages Data Fetch\\\\\\\\n  – Home highlights, Bylaws PDF link, Schools list (GraphQL static).\\\\\\\\n  – News & Events list (public subset).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 4 – Auth0 Integration & Guards\\\\\\\\n  – Install `@auth0/auth0-react`; create `AuthProvider`.\\\\\\\\n  – Build `withAuth` HOC; secure `/dues`, `/annual-meetings`, article detail if `isResidentOnly`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 5 – Resident Features\\\\\\\\n  – Dues page: placeholder to call `/api/pay` (stripe) and fetch DuesConfig for amount.\\\\\\\\n  – Annual Meeting listing downloads from Strapi media URLs.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 6 – Incremental Static Regeneration & Revalidation\\\\\\\\n  – ISR for article list & details every 5 min; webhook from Strapi triggers revalidate API endpoint.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 7 – Accessibility & QA\\\\\\\\n  – axe-core audit, screen-reader testing, keyboard focus traps.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPhase 8 – Production Deployment\\\\\\\\n  – CMS → Railway (Docker) + Postgres add-on + S3 for uploads.\\\\\\\\n  – Web → Vercel w/ ENV (`STRAPI_URL`, `AUTH0_DOMAIN`, `AUTH0_CLIENT_ID`, etc.).\\\\\\\\n  – Cloudfront / Vercel CDN handles docs & images via S3/Vercel asset pipeline.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDependencies / Hand-offs\\\\\\\\n• Auth Team delivers tenants, callback URLs, RBAC rules.\\\\\\\\n• DevOps provides Postgres, S3 creds, secure ENV injection.\\\\\\\\n• Payments team for Stripe endpoint.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEnd of Report.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_devops_sync\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order devops-sync-v2 from agent 2: **Re-Aligned DevOps, Hosting & DEP – Vercel + Render + AWS S3 (Staging / Prod)**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Hosting Summary\\\\\\\\n   • **Front-end** (Next.js): Vercel Hobby plan – zero cost, auto-SSL, GitHub integration, preview deployments, analytics.\\\\\\\\n   • **CMS / API**: Strapi on Render Web Service  \\\\\\\\n        – Prod: Starter instance (1 CPU, 2 GB) ‑ $7/mo  \\\\\\\\n        – Staging: Free instance (auto-sleep) ‑ $0  \\\\\\\\n   • **Database**: Render Managed Postgres  \\\\\\\\n        – Prod: Starter 1 GB ‑ $7/mo (daily backups, 7-day retention)  \\\\\\\\n        – Staging: Free Dev DB (sleeping) ‑ $0\\\\\\\\n   • **Docs / Assets**: AWS S3 (per-env buckets) + CloudFront optional later.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. CI/CD & Environment Segregation\\\\\\\\n   • **Git flow**: `main`→prod, `develop`→staging.  \\\\\\\\n   • Vercel Git integration auto-deploys both branches to matching domains:  \\\\\\\\n        – prod:  https://www.<domain>  \\\\\\\\n        – staging: https://staging.<domain>  \\\\\\\\n   • Render Blueprints watch GitHub; push to `develop` builds staging app; merge to `main` triggers prod build.\\\\\\\\n   • GitHub Actions runs unified test suite (frontend + backend) before merge; status required.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Backups & DR\\\\\\\\n   • Render DB daily backups (included).  \\\\\\\\n   • **Weekly pg_dump → S3** via scheduled GitHub Action (`cron-backup.yml`) storing dumps in `/backups/YYYY-MM` folder, S3 lifecycle 30-day retention.  \\\\\\\\n   • S3 versioning + Cross-Region Replication toggle available for future.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Monitoring / Logging / Alerts\\\\\\\\n   • Vercel & Render provide real-time logs; export via `vercel logs` / `render logs`.  \\\\\\\\n   • **Sentry**: browser SDK in Next.js, Node SDK in Strapi; DSNs kept as secrets.  \\\\\\\\n   • **UptimeRobot** free plan pinging prod & staging every 5 min (HTTPS + keyword).  \\\\\\\\n   • Render health-checks + notification (>80% CPU, >512 MB swap) to Ops email.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. Security Hardening\\\\\\\\n   • Vercel / Render auto-TLS (Let’s Encrypt).  \\\\\\\\n   • GitHub Dependabot + Snyk OSS weekly scan.  \\\\\\\\n   • Render firewall: only 443 ingress; Postgres restricted to internal service network.  \\\\\\\\n   • AWS S3 bucket policy: private, HTTPS-only, IAM user with least-privilege PUT/GET for backups.\\\\\\\\n   • Enforce MFA: GitHub, AWS IAM, Render, Vercel.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6.