ice type, branch, dockerfile path, env vars (placeholders)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-4  – Vercel Setup (CLI)\\\\\\\\n  vercel login  # browser auth\\\\\\\\n  vercel link   # in frontend repo\\\\\\\\n  vercel project env add API_URL https://strapi-$ENV.onrender.com --env $ENV\\\\\\\\n  vercel project env add SENTRY_DSN_FRONTEND $SENTRY_DSN --env $ENV\\\\\\\\n  vercel env pull .env.local --yes  # sync local\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-5  – GitHub Secrets / Variables\\\\\\\\n  gh secret set AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID_STG  <output AWS_ACCESS_KEY_staging>\\\\\\\\n  gh secret set AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_STG  <output AWS_SECRET_KEY_staging>\\\\\\\\n  gh secret set AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID_PROD <output AWS_ACCESS_KEY_prod>\\\\\\\\n  gh secret set AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_PROD <output AWS_SECRET_KEY_prod>\\\\\\\\n  gh secret set SENTRY_DSN             $SENTRY_DSN_BACK\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-6  – CI / GitHub Actions\\\\\\\\n  # .github/workflows/ci.yml (lint+unit tests)\\\\\\\\n  # .github/workflows/cron-backup.yml (weekly pg_dump → S3)\\\\\\\\n  git add .github && git commit -m \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ci & backup pipelines\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" && git push\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-7  – Domain & SSL (if custom domain)\\\\\\\\n  vercel domains add www.<domain>\\\\\\\\n  render custom-domain add strapi-prod <api.<domain>>\\\\\\\\n  # ACME challenge automated by providers\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-8  – Monitoring\\\\\\\\n  curl -X POST https://uptimerobot.com/api/ ...  # create monitors via API (script in infra/monitoring.sh)\\\\\\\\n  # Sentry DSNs already active via env vars.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSTEP-9  – Verification\\\\\\\\n  vercel --prod  # trigger production build\\\\\\\\n  render deploy strapi-prod\\\\\\\\n  curl https://www.<domain>/health   # expect 200 OK\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAll steps deterministic given valid tokens.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n9. Planning-Phase Deliverables\\\\\\\\n  • infra/terraform/ (S3 & IAM module)\\\\\\\\n  • render/strapi-*.yaml  (blueprint files)\\\\\\\\n  • .github/workflows/{ci.yml,cron-backup.yml}\\\\\\\\n  • docs/monitoring.sh (optional helper)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nReady to proceed to Execution when approved.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-26T18:47:08.656Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###phaseExec1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"All Director-rank agents have delivered harmonized, domain-specific DEPs. I have merged these into a single, end-to-end Deterministically Executable Plan that installs the complete HOA website using Vercel (Next.js), Render (Strapi + Postgres), Auth0, and AWS S3. The plan enumerates every step, flags all non-deterministic outputs for capture, and clearly defines inter-module dependencies. We are ready to shift from Planning to Execution.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"MASTER DEP – HOA WEBSITE (Vercel / Render / Auth0 / AWS S3)\\\\nSymbols: (V)=value captured deterministically; (NV)=provider-generated value recorded for later use.\\\\nPrereqs: Local workstation w/ Node 18, yarn, git, awscli, vercel-cli, render, terraform, jq.\\\\n----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n0.  Repositories\\\\n    0.1  git clone git@github.com:<org>/hoa-site.git   (frontend)\\\\n    0.2  git clone git@github.com:<org>/hoa-cms.git    (backend)\\\\n    0.3  git clone git@github.com:<org>/hoa-infra.git  (infra)\\\\n\\\\n1.  Auth0 Tenant  (run once)\\\\n    1.1  auth0 tenants create hoa-portal-prod          → TENANT_ID  (NV)\\\\n    1.2  auth0 apps create spa hoa-next --callbacks https://hoa.example.org/api/auth/callback/auth0 --logout-urls https://hoa.example.org/ --type spa → CLIENT_ID/SECRET (V)\\\\n    1.3  auth0 apps create m2m hoa-strapi --audience https://api.hoa.example.org → M2M_CLIENT_ID/SECRET (V)\\\\n    1.4  auth0 apis create hoa-api --identifier https://api.hoa.example.org --signing-alg RS256\\\\n    1.5  auth0 roles create resident; auth0 roles create board; assign scopes read:docs (resident) / admin:all (board).\\\\n\\\\n2.  AWS S3 & IAM via Terraform (hoa-infra)\\\\n    2.1  terraform -chdir=terraform init\\\\n    2.2  for ENV in staging prod; do\\\\n           terraform workspace select $ENV || terraform workspace new $ENV\\\\n           terraform apply -var=\\\\\\\"env=$ENV\\\\\\\" -auto-approve   # creates bucket, IAM user\\\\n         done\\\\n         → S3_BUCKET_$ENV, AWS_ACCESS_KEY_$ENV, AWS_SECRET_KEY_$ENV (V)\\\\n\\\\n3.  Render Services (Strapi + Postgres)\\\\n    3.1  render blueprint apply -f render/strapi-staging.yaml   → RENDER_SERVICE_ID_STG (V)  (DB_URL_STG NV)\\\\n    3.2  render blueprint apply -f render/strapi-prod.yaml      → RENDER_SERVICE_ID_PROD (V)  (DB_URL_PROD NV)\\\\n\\\\n4.  Vercel Front-End\\\\n    4.1  cd hoa-site && vercel link                           → VERCEL_PROJECT_ID (V)\\\\n    4.2  vercel env add PROD  API_URL https://api.hoa.example.org\\\\n         vercel env add PROD  AUTH0_*  (values from step 1)\\\\n         vercel env add PROD  NEXTAUTH_SECRET $(openssl rand -hex 32)  (NV)\\\\n    4.3  vercel env add STAGING equivalents (api-staging URL)\\\\n\\\\n5.  Strapi Configuration\\\\n    5.1  cd hoa-cms\\\\n         yarn add strapi-provider-upload-aws-s3 jwks-rsa jsonwebtoken\\\\n    5.2  echo \\\\\\\"AUTH0_DOMAIN=${TENANT_ID}.us.auth0.com\\\\\\\" >> .env\\\\n         echo \\\\\\\"AWS_S3_BUCKET=$S3_BUCKET_prod\\\\\\\" >> .env\\\\n         # commit auth0 middleware (+ content types) – deterministic file set\\\\n    5.3  git commit -m \\\\\\\"feat: auth0 + s3 integration\\\\\\\" && git push\\\\n    5.4  Render auto-redeploy; verify https://api.hoa.example.org/admin (manual Super-Admin creation).\\\\n\\\\n6.  GitHub Secrets / CI\\\\n    6.1  gh secret set VERCEL_TOKEN              # personal token (NV)\\\\n    6.2  gh secret set RENDER_TOKEN              # personal token (NV)\\\\n    6.3  gh secret set AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID_STG     $AWS_ACCESS_KEY_staging\\\\n    6.4  gh secret set AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_STG $AWS_SECRET_KEY_staging\\\\n    6.5  gh secret set AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID_PROD    $AWS_ACCESS_KEY_prod\\\\n    6.6  gh secret set AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_PROD $AWS_SECRET_KEY_prod\\\\n    6.7  Push .github/workflows/{vercel.yml,render.yml,backup.yml}\\\\n\\\\n7.  DNS & SSL\\\\n    7.1  Route 53 records:\\\\n         hoa.example.org  → CNAME cname.vercel-dns.com.       (front-end)\\\\n         api.hoa.example.org → A record Render IP.\\\\n    7.2  CloudFront distribution (optional public docs) → CNAME cdn.hoa.example.org → update Strapi `MEDIA_CDN_URL`.\\\\n\\\\n8.  Monitoring & Alerts\\\\n    8.1  curl -XPOST https://uptimerobot.com/api/newMonitor … for\\\\n         – https://hoa.example.org/healthz\\\\n         – https://api.hoa.example.org/healthz\\\\n    8.2  Sentry: set DSN env vars in Vercel & Render.\\\\n\\\\n9.  Smoke Tests (deterministic)\\\\n    9.1  curl -I https://hoa.example.org | grep \\\\\\\"200\\\\\\\"\\\\n    9.2  TOKEN=$(auth0 test-token …resident…) &&\\\\n         curl -H \\\\\\\"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\\\\\\\" https://api.hoa.example.org/docs/signed-url | jq -e .url\\\\n\\\\n10. Admin Training & Handoff\\\\n     10.1  Record 5-min Loom demonstrating Strapi post & file upload.\\\\n     10.2  Deliver 1Password vault entry with Auth0, Vercel, Render credentials.\\\\n----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nVARIABLE OUTPUTS SUMMARY\\\\nTENANT_ID, CLIENT_ID/SECRET, M2M_CLIENT_ID/SECRET, VERCEL_PROJECT_ID, NEXTAUTH_SECRET, S3_BUCKET_{staging,prod}, AWS_ACCESS/SECRET KEYS, RENDER_SERVICE_ID_{STG,PROD}, DB_URL_{STG,PROD}, VERCEL_TOKEN, RENDER_TOKEN, SENTRY_DSN_FRONT/BACK.\\\\nAll subsequent CLI steps are deterministic once these values are set.\\\"\\n}\\n###phaseExec1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-26T18:48:51.117Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [